ed Screen</source><year>2001</year>;<volume>8</volume>:<fpage>197</fpage>-202.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11743036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hakama M, Hoff G, Kronborg O, Pahlman L. Screening for colorectal cancer. <source>Acta Oncol</source><year>2005</year>;<volume>44</volume>:<fpage>425</fpage>-39.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16118076</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hakama M, Pukkala E, Soderman B, Day N. Implementation of screening as a public health policy: issues in design and evaluation. <source>J Med Screen</source><year>1999</year>;<volume>6</volume>:<fpage>209</fpage>-16.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10693068</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal">Allison JE, Sakoda LC, Levin TR, Tucker JP, Tekawa IS, Cuff T, et al. Screening for colorectal neoplasms with new fecal occult blood tests: update on performance characteristics. <source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>99</volume>:<fpage>1462</fpage>-70.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17895475</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal">Allison JE, Tekawa IS, Ransom LJ, Adrain AL. A comparison of fecal occult-blood tests for colorectal-cancer screening. <source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1996</year>;<volume>334</volume>:<fpage>155</fpage>-9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8531970</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal">Guittet L, Bouvier V, Mariotte N, Vallee JP, Arsene D, Boutreux S, et al. Comparison of a guaiac based and an immunochemical faecal occult blood test in screening for colorectal cancer in a general average risk population. <source>Gut</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>56</volume>:<fpage>210</fpage>-4.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16891354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ahlquist DA. Molecular stool screening for colorectal cancer. Using DNA markers may be beneficial, but large scale evaluation is needed. <source>BMJ</source><year>2000</year>;<volume>321</volume>:<fpage>254</fpage>-5.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10915110</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hoff G, Bretthauer M. The science and politics of colorectal cancer screening. <source>PLoS Med</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>3</volume>(1):<fpage>e36</fpage>; quiz e104.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16383349</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hoff G, Thiis-Evensen E, Grotmol T, Sauar J, Vatn MH, Moen IE. Do undesirable effects of screening affect all-cause mortality in flexible sigmoidoscopy programmes? Experience from the Telemark polyp study 1983-1996. <source>Eur J Cancer Prev</source><year>2001</year>;<volume>10</volume>:<fpage>131</fpage>-7.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11330453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Scholefield JH, Moss SM. Faecal occult blood screening for colorectal cancer. <source>J Med Screen</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>9</volume>:<fpage>54</fpage>-5.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12133920</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">UK Colorectal Cancer Screening Pilot Group. Results of the first round of a demonstration pilot of screening for colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom. <source>BMJ</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>329</volume>:<fpage>133</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15237087</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="other"><source>IARC Handbooks of cancer prevention. Cervix cancer screening</source> Lyon: IARC Press, <year>2005</year></citation></ref><ref id="ref26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brenner H, Hoffmeister M, Arndt V, Haug U. Gender differences in colorectal cancer: implications for age at initiation of screening. <source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>96</volume>:<fpage>828</fpage>-31.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17311019</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><notes notes-type="citation-text"><p><bold>Cite this as: </bold><italic>BMJ</italic> 2008;337:a2261</p></notes></back></article>